---
import { DungeonQuests } from "../features/dungeonQuests/index.ts";
import GuideLayout from "../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const updater = new URL(`${base}update.ps1`, Astro.site).href;
---

<GuideLayout slug="dungeon-quests">
  <h2>Dungeon quests</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    In Forever, dungeon enemies give little experience, so the quests are what make a run worth it. Pick a dungeon,
    follow the stops in order, and mark each quest as you pick it up and finish it. Only Horde and both-faction quests
    are listed.
  </p>
  <details class="dd" id="addon">
    <summary>Get the in-game addon (shows your real quest status)</summary>
    <p>
      Bear Tank Codex is an addon built from this guide. Type <code>/btq</code> in game or click the bear button on your minimap. It has three tabs:
      <b>Now</b> (where to quest, what to train and which talent to take at your level), <b>Dungeons</b> (these quests
      with your real status) and <b>Professions</b> (your next rank and what to craft, counted from your bags).
    </p>
    <h4>Install on Windows (recommended)</h4>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Open PowerShell: press the Windows key, type <code>powershell</code> and press Enter.</li>
      <li>
        Paste this line and press Enter:
        <pre>irm {updater} | iex</pre>
      </li>
      <li>
        It finds your WoW: Forever folder (or asks once), installs the addon, and offers to check for updates every
        time you log in to Windows. It also removes the old BearTankQuests addon if you had it.
      </li>
      <li>Log in to the game (or type <code>/reload</code>) and type <code>/btq</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <h4>Install by hand</h4>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><a href={`${base}BearTankCodex.zip`} download>Download BearTankCodex.zip</a>.</li>
      <li>
        Unzip it into <code>World of Warcraft\_forever_\Interface\AddOns</code>, so you end up with
        <code>Interface\AddOns\BearTankCodex</code>. Delete the old <code>BearTankQuests</code> folder if you have it.
      </li>
      <li>Log in (or type <code>/reload</code>) and type <code>/btq</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="small muted">
      The addon also colors dungeon quests in your quest log and quest tracker with the dungeon's color, and their
      tooltip names the dungeon. Type <code>/btq tags</code> to turn this off or on. Click the bear button on your minimap
      to open the addon, or drag it to move it (<code>/btq minimap</code> hides it). If WoW lists it as out of date on the
      AddOns screen, tick "Load out of date AddOns".
    </p>
  </details>
  <DungeonQuests client:load />
</GuideLayout>
